coder › Implemented `toRoman`/`fromRoman` on branch `work/roman-numerals`.

Changes:
- `src/roman.ts`: `toRoman` uses a greedy value table (M, CM, D, CD, C, XC, L, XL, X, IX, V, IV, I); throws `RangeError` for non-integers, <1, or >3999. `fromRoman` uppercases input, rejects empty/unknown chars with `SyntaxError` naming the text, sums with subtractive pairing, then re-encodes via `toRoman` and requires the canonical form to match (rejects IIII, VX, IC, etc., including out-of-range totals); mixed/lower case accepted.
- `src/roman.test.ts`: tests for single symbols, additive forms, subtractive forms (incl. 1994, 3999), `toRoman` RangeError cases, `fromRoman` case-insensitivity, `SyntaxError` cases checking the message names the text, and full 1–3999 `fromRoman(toRoman(n)) === n` round-trip.

Decisions not in the request: `fromRoman` validates by canonical re-encode (strict standard form only); error messages are `Invalid Roman numeral: "<text>"` so the text is always named; empty string is a `SyntaxError` per spec rather than a type error; round-trip test covers all 3999 values.

